@TITLE@ QilinRecomp for Windows (64-bit)
==========================================

@FULL_TITLE@ (@STUDIO@), recompiled to run natively: the game's own program
translated into C++ and compiled for your PC, drawn with Vulkan.

No game data is included. You need your own copy of the game: @RELEASE@,
extracted into a folder with Dolphin.


Your game folder
----------------
In Dolphin, right-click the game in the list, choose Properties, open the
Filesystem tab, right-click the disc at the top and choose Extract Entire
Disc, and pick an empty folder. The folder you need is the one holding
"sys" and "files": if Dolphin made a DATA folder inside the one you picked,
it is that DATA folder.


Playing
-------
1. Unzip the download anywhere. Building the game needs about 2 GB free.
2. Open the folder and double-click "Play @TITLE@.exe".
3. Click "Choose your extracted disc" and pick the folder above, or drag it
   onto the window. It tells you straight away if it is the wrong game,
   another region or another revision.
4. Wait for the first build: a few minutes (up to 15 on a slower PC). Your
   game files never leave your PC.
5. Click Play. The window hides while the game runs. "Add a desktop
   shortcut" puts Play @TITLE@ on your desktop.

After that, Play @TITLE@.exe remembers your folder (even in a new download
folder), and Play starts the game straight away. After an update it builds
the game again first, recompiling only what changed.

The game's output is in work\run.log and work\run-errors.log, and the
build's in work\build.log; the game also keeps punchout.log beside its
settings (below). Send them when reporting a problem.

If Windows says "Windows protected your PC": More info, then Run anyway.
(The download isn't signed.) Or before unpacking, right-click the zip,
Properties, tick Unblock, OK.

Needs: Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and a graphics driver with Vulkan 1.3
(any recent NVIDIA, AMD or Intel driver).


Controls
--------
A Wii Remote held sideways, buttons only (no motion controls).

  Xbox controller      Keyboard        Wii Remote
  D-pad, left stick    arrows          dodge, duck, block
  B                    Z               1 (left punch)
  A                    X               2 (right punch)
  X or Y               C, Space        A (Star Punch, OK)
  Start / Back         Enter / Bksp    + / -
  Guide                H               HOME
  right stick          mouse           the pointer (left click is A)

Back + Start together, or F1 or Esc: the settings menu (the game pauses):
controls (set by pressing them), a second player for Head-to-Head, the
picture (size, a CRT look, internal resolution, filtering), full screen,
the game's language and widescreen. Alt+Enter or F11: full screen. F3: the
frame rate.

Settings, saves and the game's log are kept in %LOCALAPPDATA%\qilin\@GAME@,
with the folder you chose and the build's cache of compiled files
(build-cache).


What's in here
--------------
Play @TITLE@.exe    chooses your extracted disc, builds the game (once) and starts it
kit\qilin.exe       the recompiler: turns the disc's @BOOT@ into C++
kit\plan.tsv        which parts of the game are recompiled, and which run natively
kit\lib, include    the prebuilt rest of the game: its runtime, the renderer,
                    sound, the window and controls (SDL3), the menu (Dear ImGui)
kit\toolchain       LLVM-MinGW, a C++ compiler for Windows (Clang)
kit\files.txt       every file this release holds (see below)
work\               made when building: the game (@EXE@), built from your
                    disc, the recompiled code, the build's files and the logs
LICENSES\           the licences of everything included

Source, changes and issues: https://github.com/Qilin1066/PunchOutWii--QilinRecomp


Updates and recovery
--------------------
"Check for updates" in Play @TITLE@.exe asks GitHub for a newer release of
@FULL_TITLE@ (it sends nothing about you or your PC). If there is one, it
downloads it, unpacks it beside this folder and swaps in the new kit and
launcher, then starts again and builds the game for the new version. If
anything fails on the way, the old version is left as it was. You can also
unzip a new download anywhere, even over this folder: it finds your folder
and the cache by itself, and at its first start it removes what an older
version left behind (the Play @TITLE@.bat of the first downloads, and
files the new kit no longer has: anything in kit\ or LICENSES\
that kit\files.txt doesn't name). Your saves and settings are never in this
folder, so nothing of yours is touched.

The game is compiled for this PC's processor; moved to another PC, it is
built again. Compiled files come from the cache when nothing they're made
from has changed. A failed build leaves the working game as it was; the one
before a new build is kept as work\@EXE@.previous until the new one has run
and closed normally. "Build again from scratch" compiles everything anew.

Before the game writes a save, the copy it replaces is kept: up to five of
each save file. The settings menu's Game page, Previous saves, restores one
and restarts (backing up the current save first).
